hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1302","On the authority of Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Haywa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Mawla Shaddad. Ibn Al-Hadi, that he witnessed Abu Hurairah, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever hears a man seeking a lost The mosque, so let him say to him: May God reward you, for mosques were not built for this.” He said: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya, saying: Abu Abdullah This is Salem Al-Dawsi, his name is Sabalan."
"1303","Harun bin Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Ibn Masoud heard “a man seeking a lost thing in... The mosque, so he became angry and insulted him, and a man said to him: You are not an indecency, Ibn Masoud. He said: We were commanded to do that.”"
